$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=16,$ we have $y≈19.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=16$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable."] ["question-1131d502-6491-586e-9e5c-4aa6c2f2c8de" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/id #uuid "657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08"] ["answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" :answer/id #uuid "b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb"] ["answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb" :answer/value "17"] ["answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" :answer/id #uuid "41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38"] ["answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38" :answer/value "18"] ["answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer/id #uuid "4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a"] ["answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a" :answer/value "19"] ["answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" :answer/id #uuid "32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15"] ["answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15" :answer/value "20"] ["answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557" :answer/id #uuid "558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557"] ["answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557" :answer/value "21"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/correct "answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/choices "answer-b8e7ccce-2e82-5e1e-8aec-fe59da6cffeb"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/choices "answer-41b26ab6-dcc5-53e7-b4be-5368fc7fcf38"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/choices "answer-4837a9be-da87-5c2a-937a-176ee878175a"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/choices "answer-32f64d86-98ef-5369-b4fb-15c220217b15"] ["answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08" :answer-field/choices "answer-558b121a-2eef-5148-999a-63dbe7a14557"] ["question-1131d502-6491-586e-9e5c-4aa6c2f2c8de" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-657377ca-bf35-54d0-beff-26dc9f7a2c08"] [17592186179654 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1131d502-6491-586e-9e5c-4aa6c2f2c8de"] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/id #uuid "bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a"] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/math-academy-id "q-133941"] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/problem "![](images/21/2130538a141293fda6b1bf07c1f0e8e5f7c347a2c688074689b1c13583a11bd2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $y$ when $x=20.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(1,23)$ and $(9,27).$*"] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/a0/a00942c18663c8e9ea2dd2c5354bbe177f7f8b35a4568c5234b9c92b844f196a.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,23)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(9,27).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{27-23}{9-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{8} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(1,23):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+b \\\\ 23 & =0.5(1)+b \\\\ 23 & =0.5+b \\\\ b & =22.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+22.5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=20$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =0.5x+22.5 \\\\  & =0.5(20)+22.5 \\\\  & =10+22.5 \\\\  & =32.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=20$ we have $y≈32.5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=20$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable."] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b"] ["answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" :answer/id #uuid "528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8"] ["answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8" :answer/value "30.5"] ["answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" :answer/id #uuid "5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e"] ["answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e" :answer/value "31"] ["answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer/id #uuid "5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4"] ["answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4" :answer/value "32.5"] ["answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" :answer/id #uuid "f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4"] ["answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4" :answer/value "33"] ["answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163" :answer/id #uuid "3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163"] ["answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163" :answer/value "34.5"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/correct "answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/choices "answer-528ae067-ae5a-58ad-a807-4a32664e9dd8"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/choices "answer-5a121c0e-eee5-5094-93d2-ed8591f7049e"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/choices "answer-5f18bd76-f921-5ef0-ab74-e55531698dd4"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/choices "answer-f96d4a56-8233-583c-bdd1-d33a53b4fcd4"] ["answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b" :answer-field/choices "answer-3177c2c7-aa42-566a-8362-fecceb1e8163"] ["question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1a665d06-44a7-566e-9ba1-44800e618b3b"] [17592186179655 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bf3f9846-0d01-5263-932f-08763c5ce37a"] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/id #uuid "73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819"] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/math-academy-id "q-133962"] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f38e64442bb383f218dede5a88740653f958864d3284ce09c3e1bb99ed7e421.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time (in hours) some college students spend studying the night before an exam and the time they spend sleeping that night. Assuming this trend continues, estimate the time a student spends studying if that student gets only $3.75$ hours of sleep.\n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear and that the trend line passes through the points $(2,7.5)$ and $(4,5).$*"] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/9e/9e1653b2acbe5c5924e2d562308b2640c64f317ed7500fba4e149c926c9205ab.png)\n\nThe trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,7.5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,5).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-7.5}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2.5)}{2} \\\\  & =-1.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1.25$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-1.25x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.25x+b \\\\ 5 & =-1.25(4)+b \\\\ 5 & =-5+b \\\\ b & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-1.25x+10.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=3.75$ into the equation above and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1.25x+10 \\\\ 3.75 & =-1.25x+10 \\\\ 1.25x & =6.25 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, the student spends approximately $5$ hours studying.\n\nNote: The point where $y=3.75$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable."] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d"] ["answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer/id #uuid "f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee"] ["answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee" :answer/value "$5$ hours"] ["answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" :answer/id #uuid "41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7"] ["answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7" :answer/value "$5.25$ hours"] ["answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" :answer/id #uuid "fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6"] ["answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6" :answer/value "$5.5$ hours"] ["answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" :answer/id #uuid "ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef"] ["answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef" :answer/value "$5.75$ hours"] ["answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897" :answer/id #uuid "7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897"] ["answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897" :answer/value "$6$ hours"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/correct "answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/choices "answer-f8e37f8a-7f29-5bb4-a7b5-9b3b74038eee"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/choices "answer-41db18df-a534-5726-b39d-8b9562beddc7"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/choices "answer-fa18fd73-7cda-5618-806a-041e5424f8a6"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/choices "answer-ac1ecf06-594b-58b4-b365-6708b2e5e0ef"] ["answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d" :answer-field/choices "answer-7378e9b9-c866-5489-8c98-278113aa0897"] ["question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b6a3ec9d-c696-5081-a8d8-ff61a574a27d"] [17592186179655 :knowledge-point/questions "question-73f7b139-c8da-5c53-9a35-10e77ca9a819"] ["question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/id #uuid "f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2"] ["question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-133942"] ["question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9aa9f94a8de990bdb8332f2efd5c8e945c9bec4847855eebc3fe7f6a3a02a175.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points. Estimate the value of $y$ when $x=23.$ \n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear, and that the trend line passes through the points $(11,8)$ and $(15,7).$*"] ["question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/worked-solution "First, using the hint, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/b9/b9dbed9bab9d769f7408006854bd0c159cb980bfa5f4441fe1b4e5753dfbc078.png)\n\nOur trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(11,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(15,7).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-8}{15-11} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)}{4} \\\\  & =-0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.25$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.25x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(11,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.25x+b \\\\ 8 & =-0.25(11)+b \\\\ 8 & =-2.75+b \\\\ b & =10.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.25x+10.75.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=23$ into the equation above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.25x+10.75 \\\\  & =-0.25(23)+10.75 \\\\  & =-5.75+10.75 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=23$ we have $y≈5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=23$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable."] ["question-f0d9aadf-c429-54b7-bed3-89ab52703eb2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9"] ["answer-ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" :answer/id #uuid "ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c"] ["answer-ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ec03f0fb-5fe8-5b76-ae17-c5f458c1c65c" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" :answer/id #uuid "0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d"] ["answer-0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0c57330b-8507-5a3c-9806-0e8c205fd13d" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" :answer/id #uuid "1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d"] ["answer-1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1803bbd6-5355-5d9a-9fb7-f4cf0aaa465d" :answer/value "4.5"] ["answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer/id #uuid "d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5"] ["answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d3eb3f93-e0e4-5ab6-ab1b-9485d4573bd5" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85" :answer/id #uuid "a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85"] ["answer-a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a236d02f-5776-5a91-b192-27c106d17a85" :answer/value "5.5"] ["answer-field-588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-588b06de-dfd6-5c5b-94a0-cddc954cebc9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answe